        "1. **Handling Variable Sizes:** Unlike raw coordinate arrays (which change size when moving from $N=2$ to $N=8$), the SOAP descriptor outputs a **fixed-size vector** (determined by $n_{\\text{max}}$, $l_{\\text{max}}$, and species count), regardless of how many atoms are in the system.\n",
        "2. **Quantifying Chemical Environment:** The distance matrix shows that the 10-atom chain and the 8-atom cubane have very different local atomic environments compared to the isolated dimer, mapping out structural phase space quantitatively.\n",
