        "\n",
        "## 🔬 Interactive Activity: Tuning SOAP Hyperparameters & Comparing Similarity Metrics\n",
        "\n",
        "In this activity, you will investigate two crucial aspects of machine learning descriptors:\n",
        "1. **Hyperparameter Sensitivity:** How changing the spatial cutoff ($r_{\\text{cut}}$) and expansion resolution ($n_{\\text{max}}, l_{\\text{max}}$) alters the mathematical fingerprint of our Hg–Te systems.\n",
        "2. **Metric Definition:** How the choice of distance or similarity metric (Cosine Distance vs. Continuous Tanimoto Coefficient) alters our quantitative view of structural similarity between the dimer, cubane, and 10-atom chain.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### Part 1: Exploring SOAP Hyperparameters\n",
        "* **Cutoff Radius ($r_{\\text{cut}}$):** Defines the local neighborhood sphere around each atom. If $r_{\\text{cut}}$ is too small (e.g., $2.0\\ \\text{Å}$), atoms won't \"see\" their neighbors beyond the immediate bond. If it's too large, computational cost explodes.\n",
        "* **Basis Resolution ($n_{\\text{max}}, l_{\\text{max}}$):** Higher values increase the resolution of the radial shells and angular spherical harmonics, resulting in a much larger (higher-dimensional) feature vector."
      ],
